--------------------
INSTRUCTIONS

This teleporting script will allow you to move anywhere around a structure. This does not teleport you to another structure, or to another playfield.

How to use:
Put down a signal causing device. The plate you stand on, seems to work best.
Once it's down, have it create a signal with a unique name. Put the name of this signal, in line 1 of this script, between the quotes.

Then, go to the location you want to appear. I recommend putting down a block. Use the 'di' command to identify the X Y and Z coordinates of that block. Then, remove the block.
Put those coordinates, into line 19 of this script. So your line should be {{#block @root.E.S X Y Z}}. 

Obviously, the LCD that this script is on must be named 'Script:' with whatever you like afterwards, so the script will execute.
I would also recommend setting this LCD to 'follow' on/off on the signal. You do not need this script to be sat looping waiting for someone to touch the pad, until someone actually touches the pad. 
This way, when you touch the pad, the LCD switches on, the script executes, and you telelport, and then the LCD and script will switch off. which is neat.
